Can read:
  /src/main/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/parser/*
  /src/main/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/SpecDDFileType.kt
  /src/test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/references/*

Must:
  Keep path, glob, and explicit symbol reference behavior separate from structure validation.
  Keep extraction, resolution, PSI reference creation, symbol lookup, warnings, and quick fixes in separate units.
  Use IntelliJ VFS and PSI APIs for navigation behavior.
  Use document-backed replacement for reference rename text updates.
  Treat unresolved path, glob, and explicit symbol diagnostics as warnings, not structural validation errors.
  Support IntelliJ rename and move refactors for exact path references.
  Support IntelliJ code-side rename discovery for exact path and explicit symbol references in SpecDD files.
  Support IntelliJ rename invoked from explicit `@` symbol references in SpecDD files without collapsing the reference text.
  Exclude glob references from automatic rename and move refactors.
  Treat explicit `@` references as symbol references.
  Do not treat backticked non-path code spans as symbol references.
  Cover each reference unit with focused tests.

Must not:
  Change parser classification rules.
  Report structural validation errors.
  Define syntax highlighting colors.
  Add user-facing settings.
